l history, Native American life, geology, and oceanography. The park also has a colorful marina and an 18-hole public golf course. On the bay's northeast edge is a pristine saltwater marsh that supports a thriving bird population.", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Bicycling<br>Birdwatching<br>Boating<br>Boat launch<br>Body surfing<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Golf course<br>Group Camping<br>Hiking<br>Museum<br>Picnic area<br>Rinse Showers<br>Surfing<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=594", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/680.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Small", "Latitude": 35.34653383, "Longitude": -120.8419937, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:14:31", "MilesFromSelected": 5, "Available": true, "AvailableFiltered": true, "ParkCategoryId": 1, "ParkActivity": 3, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 1, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-22T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 10, "IsRestrictionValid": true, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": true}, {"PlaceId": 679, "Name": "Montana De Oro SP", "Description": "Montana de Oro State Park features over 8,000 acres of rugged cliffs, secluded sandy beaches,\r\n coastal plains, streams, canyons, and hills - with 1,347-foot Valencia Peak. Naturalists and backpackers enjoy the solitude and \r\n freedom found along the park trails. There are also mountain biking and equestrian trails. The best-known beach is Spooner's Cove,\r\n across from the campground. The park's name (Mountain of Gold) comes from the golden wildflowers that bloom in spring.\r\n  Wildlife in the park includes black tailed deer and the black oystercatcher. The park includes primitive and equestrian campsites.", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Bicycling<br>Boating<br>Body surfing<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Hiking<br>Horseback riding<br>Picnic area<br>Scuba diving<br>Surfing<br>Visitor Center<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=592", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/679.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Medium", "Latitude": 35.26388889, "Longitude": -120.8622222, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:14:31", "MilesFromSelected": 10, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": true, "ParkCategoryId": 1, "ParkActivity": 1, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-24T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 7, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 713, "Name": "Hearst San Simeon SP", "Description": "Enjoy the scenic beauty of the Pacific Ocean while camping at San Simeon Creek Campground (water + showers) or Washburn Campground (water fill-up in lower campground + no showers).  This tranquil getaway has many recreational options.   Beach is closed to dogs for the protection of the threatened Snowey Plover shorebird.  ", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Birdwatching<br>Boating<br>Boat launch<br>Body surfing<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Hiking<br>Picnic area<br>Scuba diving<br>Surfing<br>Swimming<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=590", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/713.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Small", "Latitude": 35.59939284, "Longitude": -121.1254548, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:14:31", "MilesFromS